# .gitignore
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES: tells Git "never track or upload these files, even
# if I accidentally try to add them." This is what protects your real
# password and personal IP address from ending up on public GitHub.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Terraform's internal tracking files — these can contain secrets in
# plain, readable text, so they must never be committed.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Your REAL variables file (has your real password + IP in it).
# The ".example" version is intentionally still tracked and uploaded —
# that one has no real secrets in it, it's just a template for others.
terraform.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example

# Common OS junk files, not related to this project
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
